hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"190","On the authority of Abu Al-Azhar, on the authority of Hauthara bin Muhammad Al-Basri, on the authority of Sufyan bin Uyaynah, on the authority of Husayn bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Urwa Ibn Al-Mughirah Ibn Shu’bah, on the authority of his father, said: I said: O Messenger of God, do you wipe over your socks? He said: “Yes, I entered them and they were pure.”"
"191","Al-Qasim bin Bishr bin Marouf narrates, Ibn Uyaynah narrates, on the authority of Zakaria, Husayn, and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Mughirah, He heard it from his father. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, do you wipe over your socks? He said: “I entered my feet and they were pure.”"
"192","We are Bundar, Bishr bin Muadh Al-Aqdi, and Muhammad bin Aban. They said: We are Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed, we are Al-Muhajir, who is the son of Mukhlid Abu Mukhlid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he “granted permission to the traveler Three days and nights, and the resident has one day and one night if he purifies himself and puts on his socks to wipe over them.”"
